# COSMOS line-ending law — so `git status` shows REAL changes, not CRLF ghosts.
#
# 🔴 WHY THIS EXISTS: the tree was built on Windows (CRLF on disk) while the git
# blobs are LF. Without this file, every session that touches the tree sees all
# ~76 files as "modified" when nothing changed — a phantom dirty tree that hides
# the one real diff and pressures a bad commit. One tree, one truth: the diff a
# session sees must be the diff that exists.
#
# Text is normalized to LF in the repo (CI runs on Linux python:3.14; a peer on a
# cold machine clones clean). Windows launch scripts stay CRLF. Binaries untouched.

* text=auto

*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf

*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.vbs   text eol=crlf

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pem   binary
*.bin   binary
